   "x": 0,
   "y": -240,
   "w": 470,
   "text": "The real mobile app at 390px — not a redrawing.\nEach frame is the page's own rendered DOM and its own compiled stylesheet, lifted out of a live render, so what you see is what the browser painted.\n\nComment anywhere and tell me what to change; I'll make it in the code and re-capture."
  },
  {
   "id": "touch-note",
   "page": "app",
   "x": 500,
   "y": -240,
   "w": 430,
   "text": "Touch sizing is ON in these frames.\nThe canvas runs in a desktop browser, where the app's `pointer: coarse` rules would not match — so the capture forces them on. Controls here are the 44px versions a phone actually gets."
  },
